course: dictionary
lesson: 14278
title: Linking words that show a contrast
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some small words join two ideas and show how they relate. Nonetheless is one of them. It means "in spite of that" or "even so". «The road was closed; nonetheless, we found another way home.» The first part says there was a problem, and the second part says the problem did not stop them.
explain: Look at the clue before the word. Something is hard, wet, or unfair, and then nonetheless shows that things still went on or turned out well. «It was raining hard. Nonetheless, the match went ahead.» The rain did not stop the match.
explain: Nonetheless is a formal word, so you will meet it mostly in books, letters and exams. When you talk, you could say «still», «even so» or «anyway» instead. To check, swap one of these in: if the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
fact: Nonetheless means in spite of that; even so; however.
fact: Nonetheless is an adverb, and it is used mostly in formal writing.
fact: It shows a contrast: one idea is a problem, and the next idea goes ahead anyway.
fact: Nonetheless means much the same as nevertheless.
fact: In speech, people often say «still», «even so» or «anyway» instead, and you may see the phrase «but nonetheless».
exercise: «The bus was late; nonetheless, we reached the match on time.» What does nonetheless mean here? | Very quickly | Before that | Because of that | *In spite of that
exercise: «It was cold outside. Nonetheless, Ella went swimming.» Which word could replace nonetheless? | Earlier | *Even so | Instead | Therefore
exercise: Mo says, «I felt ill, but nonetheless I went to school.» What job does nonetheless do? | *It shows he went anyway, despite feeling ill | It tells the time | It shows a list of things | It names a place
test: «The hill was steep and the wind was strong; nonetheless, the children reached the top.» What does nonetheless show? | *That they still did it, in spite of the problems | That they gave up | That it was night | That the hill was short
test: Which word can you swap for nonetheless in «The rain was heavy; nonetheless, the picnic went ahead»? | Underneath | *Anyway | Sadly | Afterwards
exam: Which word means the same as nonetheless? | Suddenly | Yesterday | Underneath | *However
